      "handoff_review": "One command-first per-user macOS control plane with source-grounded guarded invocation, focus/display sessions, capability evidence and installed agent-contract seams. The active registry contains only project; four child JSON contracts remain unregistered drafts and are preserved as such. Exact targeting combines app/PID/launch/window identities. Task approval is locked, expiry/digest-bound and consumed once. Lifecycle interlock blocks unavailable healthy-daemon drains, with explicit legacy exception and unhealthy recovery kept distinct. Focus verification consumes independent window observations, not action returns. Capability readiness does not dispatch/promote. Browser completion remains orchestrator_declared. Skill installer stages and restores replaced payloads and verifies canonical/projection identities. Existing live release gate still expects legacy approval evidence; README explicitly preserves that blocked gate pending its separate migration. Exact build, launcher, fixture and runtime support paths are included; their presence is not independent behavioral proof. Installed runtime parity fixtures do not alone establish redacted release evidence; that behavior remains an explicit unbound proof gap.",
